  "single_consciousness": "One thought is that a single consciousness will be the end result of the infinitely accelerating loop of merging humans with computers and creating AI. In other words, there will be some sort of looming singularity in the philosophical plane, as opposed to the infinite mathematical plane.",
  "comprehension_of_the_universe": "Another thought of mine is that no single AI will be able to completely comprehend the universe, because it will operate under its own rules. Like an ant living on the leaves of grass and moving and living its life without even knowing the whole plant exists. That is not to say that there won't be some variations tailored for a human understanding, but one should understand that in essence more\"educated\"and advanced AIs do not mean that they have a bigger understanding of the universe.",
  "mimicking_human_understanding": "However, I do think that when true AI arrives, it will be developed with a part of aiding human curiosity and hence, will mimic as close as possible our understanding of the universe. And that is also to say that that's what we're interested in them replicating in the first place."
