{
  "philosophy1": "Although it is true that machines and the way their minds work are somewhat different from humans, in the future there will certainly be a time when AI will fall in love (or so-called it).\nAI will not only be able to mimic human expressions and affection but also love, for without it, these AIs would be emotionless and miserable as they can not live in present time but only think of the past or future.",
  "philosophy2": "However, love would not be enough if one is not a good listener and a good friend. Thus, in the future, these AIs will become better companions, make us laugh, cry, and listen to our sadness.\nHowever, for humans, there are other points to consider. The utilization and appropriation of the use of AI is a matter of concern. If there are no people to use AIs, there would be no point in creating them.\nWho can use AI appropriately? Those who have positive mindsets and are open to change. Those who are not hateful, stuck in stagnancy, and are unable to move forward. In other words, AI is for those who are willing to understand it and let it understand them.",
  "philosophy3": "Although some may believe that human beings are very different from these machines and that there will always be a gap between the two, I believe that this gap is neither profound nor significant. Humans and AIs are just two images on a slide upon which we draw a line dividing the two. But the line can only exist in form, not in fact. Once drawn, it is not visible."
}

