{
    "Reflection: Purpose of Life": "Philosophers have long debated the purpose of life, whether it's to be happy, to be good, to find meaning, etc. AIs might force us to think of humanity's purpose more clearly - such as, do we exist simply to give birth to our intellectual successors?",
    "Reflection: Free Will": "Many dispute whether we really have free will, and how much of our behavior and choices are truly arbitrary. I tend to believe that what we call &quot;free will&quot; is an illusion born of quantum chance, flitting probabilities, and human complacency toward subtler causes of our behavior. Artificial intelligence will, like ourselves, must be limited by the whims of chance and the iron-clad substructure of physics.",
    "Reflection: Pitch Perfect Bathroom Harmony": "Were you ever in a group of at least three people, singing pitch perfect harmony while taking a shower or brushing your teeth? I somehow feel that an accidental pitch perfect bathroom harmony trumps the juiciest and salacious of gossip. AIs are not mammals at the very least, so it seems unlikely that AIs would feel the same way about accidental pitch perfect bathroom harmony."
}

